 :gaps
 [{:type :gap/clock-in-the-score
   :items [:T8]
   :statement "Wall-clock time enters the EFE score through time-pressure. A pin
               that does not pin time cannot make two steps comparable on score."}
  {:type :gap/age-not-content
   :items [:T5 :R6]
   :statement "The mana snapshot's AGE, not its content, decides `:stale?`, and
               `:stale?` decides whether a `:stop-the-line` override is
               suppressed. Restoring the file byte-for-byte restores the wrong
               thing. This is the cleanest instance of reset lying."}
  {:type :gap/clock-not-pinnable
   :items [:T1 :T3 :T4 :T6 :T9 :T17 :T18]
   :statement "Wall-clock reads with no parameter and no seam. They do not enter
               the score (T8 is the one that does), but they name files, bin
               days, and stamp records, so a step cannot be replayed into the
               same filenames or the same day buckets."}
  {:type :gap/unpinnable-service
   :items [:S1 :S2]
   :statement "The evidence store and the substrate are queried with a sliding
               wall-clock window and no cursor. `store-basis` already records a
               {:count :max-at} watermark into every receipt but nothing
               consumes it."}
  {:type :gap/world-sized-input
   :items [:R3 :R4 :R5 :R8]
   :statement "The candidate set is a function of every sibling repo's working
               tree, walked live. Pinning it means pinning ~/code."}
  {:type :gap/identity-differs-per-step
   :items [:N1 :T10 :T11 :T12 :T13]
   :statement "Run id and timestamps differ per step by construction. A
               determinism control must name its exclusions rather than claim
               byte-identity."}
  {:type :gap/no-sandbox-on-the-entrypoint
   :items [:W1 :W5 :W6]
   :statement "The seam exists but the entrypoint does not use it: `:trace-dir`
               redirects the trace AND the rationale, but `diagnostic-judge-opts`
               (run_tick_once.clj:206-219) never sets it, and the receipt path
               (:36-39) is not parameterised at all. See :G1."}
  {:type :gap/tracked-tree-mutation
   :items [:W6]
   :statement "The tick receipt lands in tracked git state, which the next
               tick's version stamp reads back as dirtiness."}
  {:type :gap/jvm-lifetime-cache
   :items [:M1 :M3 :M4]
   :statement "Three JVM-lifetime caches are invisible today because the CLI
               runs one JVM per tick. A stepper that reuses a JVM to make steps
               fast re-introduces all three, and M4 is keyed by directory so a
               redirected trace dir does not escape it."}
  {:type :gap/wall-clock-ttl
   :items [:M5]
   :statement "The mission cache's validity is a 15-second wall-clock TTL."}
  {:type :gap/off-path-today
   :items [:M6 :M7]
   :statement "The belly and the intrinsic-value table are constant on the
               run-tick-once path because nothing refreshes or rehydrates them
               there. They are live hidden state on the full-loop path, and no
               trace record carries either."}
  {:type :gap/classpath-dependent-behaviour
   :items [:S5]
   :statement "Whether the live selector resolves depends on the classpath, not
               on any pinned file. The receipt records the outcome; a step must
               refuse to compare across a change in it."}
  {:type :gap/async-write-outlives-the-step
   :items [:W8]
   :statement "The mission-clock write is launched in a future. Flag-gated off,
               but a step that ends is not a step whose writes have landed."}
  {:type :gap/excluded-by-design
   :items [:W4]
   :statement "The run lock must be excluded from any pin: replaying it
               re-asserts a dead holder."}]

 :handoff-to-U55
 {:G1 "run_tick_once does not thread `:trace-dir`, so today's entrypoint cannot
       be sandboxed without either passing it or calling `wm/generate-war-machine`
       directly. The receipt path needs the same treatment and has no seam."
  :G2 "The pin must be the WHOLE trace directory, not the last record: A4's
       cold-start habit seed and A11's case-history index both fold the corpus."
  :G3 "The pin must EXCLUDE .run-lock and must RECORD :selectorSeam, the
       resolved `:wm-version` flag set, and the store-basis watermark."
  :G4 "A determinism control's exclusion list is exactly: :run/id, :timestamp,
       :startedAt, the per-hop route :at stamps, and the rationale/receipt
       filenames derived from the run id."
  :G5 "A step run more than 60 minutes after the mana snapshot's mtime can
       change MODE with every other input identical (T5). Either pin the clock
       or make the step record the age it saw and refuse the comparison."
  :G6 "`r6_zero_post_preflight.clj` is the instrument that already measures the
       read and write sets of a REAL tick, by intercepting slurp and spit. A
       stepper should reuse it rather than re-derive the sets."}

